WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 6: My Five Senses.

2
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:10.920
In this unit, your child learns about their five senses
— seeing, hearing, smelling, tasting and touching —

3
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.760
and the body parts we use for each one.

4
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:21.120
They learn describing words (soft, loud, sweet,
cold) and start to compare things (a tree is tall,

5
00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:22.220
a building is taller).

6
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:23.720
Most of all,

7
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.300
they explore the world around them and learn to be curious
and thankful for all the wonderful things they can sense.

8
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:36.200
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:44.420
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
the five senses: see, hear, smell, taste, touch.

10
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:51.320
you will also point to and name the body
parts we use: eyes, ears, nose, tongue, hands.

11
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.220
you will also say which sense goes with
which body part (“i see with my eyes”).

12
00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.040
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:05.720
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: see, hear, smell, taste, touch, eyes.

14
00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:11.040
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.460
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:20.440
The reading sequence includes Amal at
the Market and Talk about My Five Senses.

17
00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.040
Read actively.

18
00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:26.720
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:30.580
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.860
The first language focus is Language pattern 1.

21
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:41.860
Listen to the model, point to the matching picture,
then say the pattern: I can see with my eyes.

22
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:49.260
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

23
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:55.460
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

24
00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:59.920
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

25
00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:03.360
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

26
00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.060
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

27
00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.520
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:15.060
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

29
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.800
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

30
00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:23.880
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
